schedule: Float as float, Int as long, work-group 256, products and transposes untiled
buffers:
  b_x: long 8 items, %x i64 [8]; constant, uploaded by the host
  b_w: long 8 items, %w i64 [8]; constant, uploaded by the host
  b_max: long 8 items, %max i64 [8]; written on the device
  b_addr: long 1 item, %addr i64 []; written on the device
  b_l: float 8 items, %l f64 [8]; constant, uploaded by the host
  b_g: float 8 items, %g f64 [8]; constant, uploaded by the host
  b_max_2: float 8 items, %max_2 f64 [8]; written on the device
  b_addr_2: float 1 item, %addr_2 f64 []; written on the device
kernels:
  k0: 8 elements, one work-item each; computes %mul %add %max; writes %max
  reduce_add_long: a tree reduction in local memory, one partial per work-group; computes %addr
  k1: 8 elements, one work-item each; computes %div %mul_2 %add_2 %max_2; writes %max_2
  reduce_add_float: a tree reduction in local memory, one partial per work-group; computes %addr_2
launches:
  1: k0(b_x, b_w, b_max) global 8 local 8: 8 elements (1 group of 8)
  2: reduce_add_long(b_max, b_addr, 8, local 2048 bytes) global 256 local 256: %addr: add 8 items to 1 partial (pass 1)
  3: k1(b_l, b_g, b_max_2) global 8 local 8: 8 elements (1 group of 8)
  4: reduce_add_float(b_max_2, b_addr_2, 8, local 1024 bytes) global 256 local 256: %addr_2: add 8 items to 1 partial (pass 1)
outputs:
  %addr from b_addr, read back by the host
  %addr_2 from b_addr_2, read back by the host
